# S08-T06: Migrate Reader / Writer to In-Repo Paths

## Objective

Accept + reader use `planning-path.ts` + epic `targetApp`. Rename or alias modules.

## App-agent preflight (MANDATORY)

- [ ] `get-file` — `totem-reader.ts`, `totem-writer.ts`, accept route
- [ ] `explain("work-control")` — API + write-back sections

## Implementation

- [ ] `planning-reader.ts` — read `.ptl`/`.pd` from `resolveSprintsDir(targetApp)`
- [ ] `planning-writer.ts` — write to same; inject protocol from `apps/{targetApp}/planning/templates/` or fallback
- [ ] Accept handler: pass `epic.targetApp` to writer
- [ ] `open-gate`: flip `.ptl` under correct in-repo path
- [ ] Keep `totem-reader.ts` / `totem-writer.ts` as re-exports OR update all imports
- [ ] Update `core/tests/unit/totem-writer.test.ts` → planning-writer
- [ ] `defineFeatureHandler('work-control')` unchanged on routes

## Done when

- [ ] Accept writes to `apps/work-control/planning/sprints/S<NN>-*.ptl` @ OPEN
- [ ] Reader returns in-repo sprint
- [ ] `bun run test` green
